Z||000000||AkursedX||11-07-2001||06:43 PM||||Well, that time a year as come, like it comes for the most of us northerners where I put my Fiero away in the garage for the Winter  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">  <BR>But, unlike last year, this year, all I did was pull an 87GT out of my garage for my winter car!!!  It's so nice having 2 Fiero's.  Needless to say, it was a very exciting day.  This was the first time that I actually got to drive the car and I'm glad that it runs well.  <P>Some sidenotes though:  My 87GT is stock height, and the suspension is all stock besides KYB's up in front.  Well let me say, it is a world of difference between that car and my 88GT.  But the 87 is so much more comfortable to drive since I'm not feeling every single bump and uneveness in the road like I did with my 88.  <P>Also, how on earth do you people drive with a spoiler on the car!?!?  That thing is such a distraction in my rearview! <BR> Tinted windows at night suck.  If the car didn't looks so good with it, I would get rid of it.  <P>As for my 88, it is going to be the recipient of an engine swap/mod this semester.  Right now I'm leaning towards a crate 3.4 with ported heads/intake, headers, borla, and all that other fun stuff.  Hopefully it'll be a 200hp+ beast by next spring/summer.<P>After I get my rims all stripped and repainted, I will post pics of my 87GT.  It's all black, with tinted windows, and the rims will be painted all black, so it's gonna look pretty sweet.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/cool.gif"><P>------------------<BR><BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigpic2_2.jpg"> ||||reg||9
